# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Simulation output (camera frames + poses, regenerated each run)
sim/output/

# Webots per-world editor state (regenerated on every open)
sim/worlds/.*.wbproj

# Claude Code local (per-machine) settings
.claude/settings.local.json
pics/*
# web/.env.example is the committed TEMPLATE (dev placeholders only, no real
# secrets) — CLAUDE.md's setup step copies it to web/.env, and docker-compose
# now fails loud without those vars, so a fresh clone needs it. The real
# web/.env stays ignored via web/.gitignore.

# Generated detection datasets (vision/dataset.py). Derived from the world's
# cars.json + a flight's frames, so they are reproducible in one command and
# would otherwise add thousands of PNGs and label files to the tree.
vision/datasets/

# ablation harness feature cache (regenerate with --refresh)
vision/diag/.ablation_cache/

# Model weights: pretrained checkpoints are downloaded on demand by ultralytics,
# and fine-tuned ones are reproducible from vision/train_detector.py + the
# tracked labels. Either way they are tens of MB of binary that git handles badly.
*.pt

# Training runs (vision/train_detector.py): weights, plots and per-epoch CSVs.
# The inputs are tracked (labels + the script + a fixed seed), so a run is
# reproducible; the outputs are not worth versioning.
vision/runs/
docs/final_doc_draft.md
docs/final_doc_review.md

# Diagnostic renders (vision/diag/*.py --out): large PNGs, all regenerable.
vision/diag/out/
